      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Bertrand I. Halperin",
        "David R. Nelson",
        "A. Peter Young"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The defect-mediated theory of two-dimensional melting established a striking example of how topological defects and universal mechanisms determine phase behavior.",
        "attribution": "Halperin and Nelson developed the central theory, while Young made a key independent contribution to its formulation and analysis.",
        "maturity": "This is a thoroughly tested and enduring body of work, with decades of experimental and theoretical development behind it.",
        "uncertainties": [
