        "Alexei Kitaev",
        "Andrew M. Steane",
        "Peter W. Shor"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction established that noise need not make quantum computation fundamentally impossible, changing the theoretical outlook for quantum information processing.",
        "attribution": "Kitaev, Steane, and Shor represent major complementary advances in fault-tolerant theory and error-correcting codes; several other researchers also shaped the field.",
        "maturity": "The principle is mathematically established and has growing experimental demonstrations, but large-scale fault-tolerant operation remains unrealized.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The timing of recognition is uncertain while practical fault tolerance is still under development.",
          "A three-person attribution must distinguish foundational ideas from subsequent breakthroughs."
        ]
      }
    },
